  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 13.92pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.8pt, 84pt, "Simultaneous, Non-Contact Measurement of Liquid and Interfacial ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 108.24pt, "Thermal Properties via a Differential Square-Pulsed Source Method")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.8pt, 151.2pt, "Tao Chen, and Puqing Jiang* ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 171.84pt, "School of Energy and Power Engineering, Huazhong University of Science and Technology, ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 192.48pt, "Wuhan, Hubei 430074, China ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 213.12pt, "*E-mail: jpq2021@hust.edu.cn ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.8pt, 254.64pt, "ABSTRACT: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(145.895pt, 254.64pt, "Accurate characterization of heat transport across solid-liquid interfaces is ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 275.28pt, "essential for thermal management in micro- and nanoscale systems. Yet existing techniques ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 295.92pt, "often require prior knowledge of liquid properties, which complicates the simultaneous ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 316.8pt, "resolution of interfacial and bulk behaviors, and lose sensitivity once interfacial conductance ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 337.44pt, "exceeds 100 MW m")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.196pt, 333.36pt, "-2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(172.86pt, 337.44pt, " K")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(183.929pt, 333.36pt, "-1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(190.593pt, 337.44pt, ". Here we present a differential square-pulsed source (DSPS) method ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 358.08pt, "that provides simultaneous, non-contact measurement of liquid thermal conductivity, ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 378.72pt, "volumetric heat capacity, and solid-liquid interfacial conductance without any predefined ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 399.6pt, "material parameters. Dual-frequency excitation combined with in-situ substrate referencing ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 420.24pt, "enables property extraction from multilayer structures, and numerical simulations show a ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 440.88pt, "typical uncertainty of about 8 % in interfacial conductance, confirming robustness. The protocol ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 461.52pt, "is validated for a wide spectrum of liquids, including oils, lubricants, aqueous electrolytes, and ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 482.4pt, "pure water, with excellent agreement with literature values for bulk properties. Analysis of the ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 503.04pt, "data set clarifies how vibrational-spectrum mismatch, ionic layering, and related interfacial ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 523.68pt, "phenomena govern heat transfer, and demonstrates that oleophilic hexadecyl silane ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 544.32pt, "modification of aluminum increases interfacial conductance by a factor of sixteen. The results ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 565.2pt, "reveal that conductance can be strongly tuned through surface wettability and chemical ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 585.84pt, "functionalization, offering direct guidelines for interface engineering. Because the approach is ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 606.48pt, "readily extendable to soft materials such as thermal-interface gels, it promises broad ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 627.12pt, "applicability in emerging interface-dominated thermal technologies. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.8pt, 648pt, "KEYWORDS")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(142.144pt, 648pt, ": thermal conductivity; volumetric heat capacity; interfacial thermal ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 668.64pt, "conductance; differential square-pulsed source (DSPS); soft materials")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.8pt, 709.92pt, "1. INTRODUCTION ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(82.8pt, 730.56pt, "Thermal transport across solid-liquid interfaces plays a critical role in the performance of ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 751.44pt, "advanced thermal management systems,")
