  #line-at(139.871pt, 182.16pt, "35")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(147.871pt, 186.24pt, " is capable of simultaneously measuring the thermal conductivity and heat ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 206.88pt, "capacity of liquids, it also suffers from limited sensitivity to interfacial conductance due to the ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 227.52pt, "low thermal conductivity of liquids—similar to the challenges faced by TDTR and FDTR. Thus, ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 248.16pt, "there remains a significant gap in techniques that can simultaneously measure liquid thermal ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 269.04pt, "conductivity, volumetric heat capacity, and ITC . ")
  #line-at(82.8pt, 289.68pt, "To address these limitations, we introduce the differential square-pulsed source (DSPS) ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 310.32pt, "method, a novel technique that enables simultaneous, non-contact measurement of liquid ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 330.96pt, "thermal conductivity, volumetric heat capacity, and solid-liquid ITC. The DSPS method is ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 351.84pt, "unique in that it does not rely on prior knowledge of the liquid heat capacity, allowing for ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 372.48pt, "versatile and accurate measurements of both the bulk and interfacial thermal properties of ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 393.12pt, "liquids. A key advantage of the DSPS method is its differential measurement strategy, which ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 413.76pt, "effectively reduces the uncertainty in ITC extraction. This method is validated across a diverse ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 434.64pt, "range of liquids, including lubricants, oils, aqueous solutions, and pure water, with excellent ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 455.28pt, "agreement with literature values for thermal conductivity and volumetric heat capacity. ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 475.92pt, "Furthermore, the DSPS method offers new insights into the role of ITC at solid-liquid interfaces, ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 496.56pt, "particularly through the investigation of surface modifications that enhance oleophilicity or ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 517.44pt, "hydrophilicity, which significantly improve interfacial heat transfer. By enabling direct and ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 538.08pt, "simultaneous measurements of these critical parameters, the DSPS method provides a powerful ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 558.72pt, "tool for understanding and optimizing interfacial thermal transport in liquid and nanoscale ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 579.36pt, "systems.  ")
