  #line-at(82.8pt, 641.52pt, "2.1. Measurement Technique and Data Processing.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0563c1"))
  #line-at(374.211pt, 641.52pt, "Figure 1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(414.387pt, 641.52pt, "a shows a schematic of ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 662.16pt, "the DSPS system. In this configuration, a function generator modulates a 458 nm pump laser ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 683.04pt, "with a square wave to induce periodic heating of the sample. Concurrently, a 785 nm probe ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 703.68pt, "laser monitors the periodic surface temperature fluctuations of the sample. When the induced ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 724.32pt, "temperature rise remains relatively modest (below approximately 10 K), the intensity variations ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 744.96pt, "of the reflected probe laser accurately follow the temperature dynamics. The reflected probe ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 765.84pt, "signal is converted into an electrical signal by a photodiode detector and subsequently analyzed ")
]

// arXiv source page 4
#original-page(595pt, 842pt, (image("graphics/page-04.png", width: 436.5pt), 78pt, 263pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.6pt, 789.84pt, "4 ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 82.08pt, "using the periodic waveform analyzer (PWA) module of a digital lock-in amplifier, extracting ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 102.72pt, "the amplitude over a complete modulation period. In periodic thermoreflectance measurements, ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 123.6pt, "PWA offers narrow-band extraction with large dynamic reserve, enabling robust ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 144.24pt, "amplitude/phase readout; in contrast, oscilloscopes have been primarily used in earlier studies ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 164.88pt, "to monitor the noise level, while PWA further facilitated precise signal extraction.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(492.266pt, 160.8pt, "36")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(500.266pt, 164.88pt, " The ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 185.52pt, "extracted amplitude data is then fitted to a heat transfer model to accurately determine the ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 206.4pt, "thermal properties of the sample. Detailed discussion on heat transfer model development is ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 227.04pt, "available in Supporting Information Section S1. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.8pt, 415.2pt, "Figure 1.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(118.616pt, 415.2pt, " (a) Schematic of the differential square pulsed source (DSPS) setup for thermal ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 435.84pt, "measurement. (b) 3D optical layout showing pump and probe beams focused onto the sample. ")
  #line-at(82.8pt, 477.36pt, "The DSPS setup is similar to FDTR, but there are key differences. In FDTR, a beamsplitter ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 498pt, "is required at the pump beam output to measure the pump phase, and the optical paths of the ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 518.64pt, "pump and probe beams must be equal to determine the phase difference between the two beams ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 539.28pt, "as a function of the pump modulation frequency. In contrast, TDTR uses two pulsed lasers with ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 560.16pt, "a controlled time delay, applying a pulsed heating source and measuring the temperature ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 580.8pt, "evolution as a function of delay time. While DSPS shares some similarities with FDTR, its ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 601.44pt, "unique advantage lies in its high signal-to-noise (SNR) ratio and the ability to achieve a wide ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 622.08pt, "range of modulation frequencies, from 1 Hz to 10 MHz. The superior SNR of SPS originates ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 642.96pt, "from measuring the amplitude signal and employing PWA-based synchronous averaging, ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 663.6pt, "which ensure robust readout even at low modulation frequencies, where FDTR phase detection ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 684.24pt, "typically fails due to phase drift and near-zero response. This capability makes DSPS ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 704.88pt, "particularly effective for measuring materials with low in-plane thermal conductivity,")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(516.4pt, 700.8pt, "35")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.8pt, 725.52pt, "anisotropic structures exhibiting three-dimensional thermal conduction,")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(422.165pt, 721.44pt, "37")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(430.165pt, 725.52pt, " multilayer films,")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(516.4pt, 721.44pt, "38")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.8pt, 746.4pt, "and convective heat transfer coefficients.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(267.698pt, 742.32pt, "39")
]

