#original-page(595pt, 842pt, (image("graphics/page-13.png", width: 327pt), 82.5pt, 497pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(291.6pt, 789.84pt, "13 ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 82.08pt, "This increase is mainly due to the solution’s elevated ionic strength, which induces ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 102.72pt, "overscreening at the aluminum surface and forms a thicker Stern layer. Simultaneously, ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 123.6pt, "penetration by Na⁺ and Cl⁻ ions disrupts the first two layers of interfacial water, weakening ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 144.24pt, "water-Al phonon coupling. The combined effect significantly hampers heat transport across the ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 164.88pt, "interface.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(115.765pt, 160.8pt, "50, 51")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(82.8pt, 185.52pt, "Conversely, the WD-40 lubricant displays an unusually small Kapitza length of about 4 nm. ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 206.4pt, "This significant reduction arises from its unique composition, primarily consisting of ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 227.04pt, "hydrogenated light distillates and carbon dioxide. The low viscosity and high fluidity of these ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 247.68pt, "hydrogenated distillates enhance interfacial wettability, creating a more uniform liquid-solid ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 268.32pt, "contact layer. Additionally, dissolved carbon dioxide further reduces surface tension, thus ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 289.2pt, "promoting stronger interfacial coupling. Collectively, these factors enhance the solid-liquid ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 309.84pt, "adhesion and sharply lower the thermal boundary resistance.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(361.372pt, 305.76pt, "28, 52")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(82.8pt, 330.48pt, "In sharp contrast, the TBP-dodecane mixture exhibits a notably large Kapitza length of ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 351.12pt, "approximately 41 nm. This substantial interfacial resistance is explained by the significant ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 372pt, "mismatch in vibrational spectra across the interface. Molecular vibrations within the liquid ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 392.64pt, "occur at markedly higher frequencies, specifically the P=O stretching mode of TBP around ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 413.28pt, "1278 cm⁻¹ (≈38 THz)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(176.281pt, 409.2pt, "53")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(184.281pt, 413.28pt, " and the C-H stretching modes of n-dodecane around 2850 cm⁻¹ (≈85 ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 433.92pt, "THz),")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(99.118pt, 429.84pt, "54")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(107.118pt, 433.92pt, " whereas aluminum's phonon spectrum extends only up to approximately 9-10 THz.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(514.4pt, 429.84pt, "55, ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 450.72pt, "56")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(78.8pt, 454.8pt, " The pronounced vibrational mismatch between the liquid and aluminum severely impedes ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 475.44pt, "phonon transmission, resulting in a significantly enhanced thermal boundary resistance.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(491.696pt, 471.36pt, "57, 58")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(82.8pt, 496.08pt, "3.3. Effect of Surface Modification on the Interface. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0563c1"))
  #line-at(369.69pt, 496.08pt, "Figure 5")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(409.422pt, 496.08pt, "c shows that the Kapitza ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 516.96pt, "length at the Al/TBP-dodecane interface is significantly larger than those of the other tested ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 537.6pt, "liquids, indicating substantially higher interfacial thermal resistance. This limitation, along with ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 558.24pt, "the broader goal of improving heat transfer at liquid-solid interfaces, motivated us to investigate ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 578.88pt, "surface modification strategies for enhancing interfacial conductance. To this end, we applied ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 599.52pt, "two distinct treatments to the aluminium surface: immersion in hexadecyltrimethoxysilane ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 620.4pt, "(HDTMS) to produce an oleophilic surface, and oxygen plasma exposure using a plasma asher ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 641.04pt, "to create a hydrophilic surface. We then evaluated the effects of these modifications using TBP-")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 661.68pt, "dodecane and water as representative liquids with contrasting polarity and practical relevance ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 682.32pt, "in thermal management applications. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0563c1"))
  #line-at(82.8pt, 703.2pt, "Figure 6")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(124.41pt, 703.2pt, "a shows that the water contact angle on untreated Al is 50°, indicating moderate ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 723.84pt, "wettability. After surface modification with HDTMS, the contact angle increased significantly ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 744.48pt, "to 104° (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0563c1"))
  #line-at(112.298pt, 744.48pt, "Figure 6")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(152.313pt, 744.48pt, "b), even one month after treatment. This increase is attributed to the formation ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 765.12pt, "of a dense hydrophobic monolayer on the Al surface by the long-chain alkyl groups of HDTMS, ")
]

