  #line-at(82.8pt, 565.44pt, "3.4. Implications and Outlook.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(254.701pt, 565.44pt, " The present dataset clarifies three actionable levers for ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 586.08pt, "engineering high-conductance solid-liquid interfaces: (i) vibrational matching, where ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 606.72pt, "minimizing spectral gaps between the liquid molecular modes and the solid phonon bandwidth ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 627.36pt, "reduces the Kapitza length; (ii) interfacial structure and charge, where ionic layering and ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 648.24pt, "overscreening can suppress energy transmission by disrupting the first hydration layers; and (iii) ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 668.88pt, "wettability and chemistry, where oleophilic or hydrophilic functionalization strengthens ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 689.52pt, "interfacial coupling, as evidenced by the approximately sixteen-fold enhancement for HDTMS ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 710.16pt, "on Al with TBP-dodecane. Practically, DSPS provides a rapid, non-contact screen for candidate ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 731.04pt, "fluids such as immersion coolants and electrolytes, as well as soft materials including TIM gels ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 751.68pt, "and PCM composites, with all three key parameters obtained in a single protocol. Our next ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 772.32pt, "work will apply this method to investigate the properties of TIMs under different pressures. In ")
]

