  #line-at(70.8pt, 82.08pt, "this scenario, the heat capacity becomes particularly important, further highlighting the ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 102.72pt, "advantage of DSPS in simultaneously measuring all three parameters. ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.8pt, 144.24pt, "4. CONCLUSIONS ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(82.8pt, 164.88pt, "In summary, we employ the differential square-pulsed source (DSPS) method to ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 185.52pt, "simultaneously measure the thermal conductivity, volumetric heat capacity, and solid-liquid ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 206.4pt, "interfacial thermal conductance of various liquid films, and the experimental results closely ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 227.04pt, "match literature values, validating the accuracy and robustness of the DSPS technique. Beyond ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 247.68pt, "benchmarking bulk properties, DSPS reveals how interfacial physics (vibrational mismatch, ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 268.32pt, "ionic effects) and surface chemistry (oleophilic and hydrophilic treatments) regulate interfacial ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 289.2pt, "conductance, offering valuable guidance for designing and optimizing solid-liquid interfaces ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 309.84pt, "and measurement approaches for liquids at the micro- and nanoscale. Looking forward, DSPS ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 330.48pt, "can be combined with in-situ surface characterization and controlled frequency/spot-size tuning ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 351.12pt, "to map the thermal properties of complex liquid-solid systems and to enable time-resolved ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 372pt, "studies during phase change. ")
